<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anselm of Havelberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1100–1158</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anselm of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havelberg">Havelberg</a> was a German churchman and theologian, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Havelberg from 1129 and archbishop of Ravenna from 1155. He served Emperors <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair</a> III and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> as envoy to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, where he debated with Greek theologians, and he took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wendish-crusade">Wendish Crusade</a> of 1147, after which he restored his see.</p></div>
